WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.480
My moustache grew through
when I was about 14

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.560
and then the rest of my beard

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.640
eventually followed
about five years later.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.840
One of the puzzles of human evolution

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.640
is why men in some populations
have kept their facial hair

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.680
when we've lost the hair
on the rest of our bodies.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.760
Now normally when we're
trying to explain a trait

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.560
that doesn’t have any
clear survival benefit

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.520
we ask whether
it can help attract a mate

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.360
but actually beards don't seem
to be important to women in general.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.160
What we do find is that beards
can help men look more dominant

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.720
and that suggest that it ties
into male-male competition.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.360
My beard makes me feel more masculine

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.480
and it makes me
want to take on the world

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.640
and people respond to me in a very,
very positive manner

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.680
when I have a beard.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.440
I'm not sure it makes me feel more of
a man, it makes me feel more like me.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.520
It helped me feel, I would say,
older or more close to my age

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.520
because I look quite young

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.680
and it helped me to look
more of a mature adult.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.720
A light beard can exaggerate
and emphasise the jawline

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.160
which is a key feature
of male facial masculinity.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.280
So a baby-faced man

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.120
can make himself look older
and more dominant by growing a beard

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.520
but there's evidence that a man
with a highly masculinised,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.080
dominant looking bone structure
can actually soften that

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.400
and look more caring
by growing a fuller beard.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.880
The recent resurgence
in Victorian aesthetics

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.080
is particularly interesting

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.760
because it's been argued
the Victorians

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.880
were reacting to earlier fashions
and the industrial revolution

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.520
by asserting a very strong,
natural form of masculinity -

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.520
including full beards as a sign
of vigour and strength.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.760
I like my beard because it's smart,
it's fashionable and it's trendy.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.080
Of course beards
can be subject to fashion.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.560
Just like any fashion, there's scope
for individual self-expression.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.800
So keeping your beard
well-groomed and glossy,

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.680
maybe styled in a particular way,

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.800
just like polishing your shoes
or choosing particular clothes,

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.520
can say something about who you are
and what you want others to see.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.360
Not so much I wanted to grow my
beard, it was mainly me being lazy.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.760
I just wake up, kind wash it
with a flannel and that's about it.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.280
I've been wanting to grow a beard
for a very long time

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.520
and it compliments my face.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.000
Facial and head hair

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.320
can be used to mark out groups
within a particular population.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.640
Now different traditions
had different specific rules

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.200
but what they all did was use hair
as a way to mark themselves out

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.440
as distinct and different.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.840
Now today
people can still use their hair

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.040
as a way of demonstrating
their piety.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.960
Each tradition
will have their own narrative

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.200
about why keeping
or shaving their hair is important,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.000
but what they all have in common

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.320
is the use of hair to make a visible
statement about group identity -

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.320
about who they are
and who they aren't.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.160
I went to Hajj, and I came back,

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.160
and for spiritual reasons
I decided to keep the beard.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.000
"As the beard gets whiter
you get more wiser,"

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.760
it's a saying, you get more wisdom.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.800
I like the length and the colour
and the way it waves in the wind.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.400
People love to compliment my beard
as well, so I'm really happy with it.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.040
Costly signalling theory is the
principle that anything in nature

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.120
which requires an investment
of time or energy

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.520
can be used to indicate
an underlying strength.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.280
Now we can see this play out
on the social level as well.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.360
Growing a long beard takes
a considerable amount of time,

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.160
maintaining a beard
requires time and effort

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.480
and that time spent can be used
as a visible symbol of commitment

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.480
to the group or to the ideology.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.160
I don't do a great deal
of maintenance on my beard,

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.680
I often mean to.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.640
But because sometimes I garden

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.480
I forget and come home
with a bird stuck in it.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.640
It almost changes my character.
I feel like I'm someone different.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.600
I feel more of a man, I feel older.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.520
It ages me.
But I can at least pretend I'm wiser.

